    <string name="minkpad_help_host_title">호스트 설정 및 키보드</string>
    <string name="minkpad_help_host_description">컨트롤러 설정에서 수신 장치의 시스템을 선택하십시오. 사전 설정은 쌍 호스트에 저장됩니다; HID는 안정적으로 운영 체제를 밝혀하지 않습니다. 메타는 Windows에서 Apple 장치 및 Windows에서 명령입니다. 소프트웨어 텍스트는 미국 레이아웃을 사용합니다. 하드웨어 키 보드 전화 라이브 편집기는 숨겨진 유지; 터치 전용 전화에 탭 유형.</string>
    <string name="minkpad_help_bluetooth_title">페어링 및 Bluetooth</string>
    <string name="minkpad_help_bluetooth_description">Start pairing opens Android’s two-minute discoverability prompt. While the countdown is running, select Pro Controller - MinkPad (your phone’s device name) in the receiving device’s Bluetooth settings and confirm the matching code. Pair new device releases the active connection before pairing another host. Android’s saved pairings are never removed automatically.\n\nWhile MinkPad runs, this phone temporarily adds Pro Controller - MinkPad before its usual Bluetooth name. For example, Titan 2 appears as Pro Controller - MinkPad (Titan 2). This compatibility identity gives Android receiving devices the responsive HID timing used by MinkPad. It uses the phone’s regular Bluetooth adapter, not a second custom BLE device. Existing accessory pairings are not erased, but headphones, watches, cars, and other accessories may disconnect, see the temporary name, or compete for the radio. Closing MinkPad restores the phone’s original Bluetooth name.\n\nOpen the top controls and tap the current receiving device to switch between saved devices. Starting MinkPad asks the most recently used device to reconnect. Manage saved devices includes a troubleshooting Disconnect action.\n\nKeyboard, mouse, and media commands go directly to the receiving device. Mink does not save or upload typed text or pointer coordinates. Nearby devices access is for Bluetooth connection and discoverability, not location. Notifications provide Open, Reconnect, and Stop; denying them does not prevent input.</string>
